    <bpmn:process id="W_W561" name="W561. Employee Attendance Exception Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Biometric/attendance system generates exception (late arrival, unauthorized absence, undertime, biometric failure, missing punch, overtime without approval)
Frequency: ~800–1,200 exceptions per day across 200 stores + 4 DCs + HQ (6,911 employees, ~12–18% exception rate)
Volume: Higher on Mondays (+25%), after holidays (+40%), during rainy season/typhoons (+30%, Metro Manila and low-lying areas), during MRT/LRT service disruptions
Owner: HR Supervisor / Store Manager (store-level)
Participants: Employee (R for self-service), Department Supervisor (R for approval), HR Supervisor, Payroll Specialist (I), Store Manager (A for store-level), Timekeeping &amp; Attendance Analyst
Source: workflow W561 — Employee Attendance Exception Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W561_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W561_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W561_Lane2" name="HR Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W561_Lane3" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W561_Lane4" name="Employee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W561_Lane5" name="CHRO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W561_End20</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W561_Start7" name="Biometric/attendance system generates exception (late arrival, unauthorized absence…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W561_Task8" name="System generates daily exception report from biometric/attendance system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System generates daily exception report from biometric/attendance system, categorized by type: (a) late arrival (punch-in after shift start + grace period); (b) unauthorized absence (no punch for full shift, no pre-filed leave); (c) undertime (punch-out before shift end); (d) missing punch (only in-punch or out-punch recorded); (e) biometric failure (system unable to read fingerprint/face); (f) unauthorized overtime (punch-out after shift end without pre-approved OT)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (daily batch at 06:00)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W561_Task9" name="HR Supervisor reviews exception dashboard prioritized by severity: unauthorized…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: HR Supervisor reviews exception dashboard prioritized by severity: unauthorized absence (critical) &gt; missing punch (high) &gt; late arrival (medium) &gt; undertime (low); dashboard shows exception count by store, department, and category with trend comparison to previous period
Responsible (R): HR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–45 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W561_Task10" name="For biometric failures: HR Supervisor verifies employee identity against…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: For biometric failures: HR Supervisor verifies employee identity against employee photo in HR master, creates manual punch entry with reason code &quot;biometric failure,&quot; obtains Department Supervisor confirmation that employee was present; submits IT ticket per W48 for biometric reader repair/maintenance; recurring biometric failures (&gt;3/month for same employee) trigger re-enrollment with alternate biometric (e.g., switch from fingerprint to face recognition)
Responsible (R): HR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min/exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W561_Task11" name="For late arrivals: Department Supervisor confirms whether late arrival was…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: For late arrivals: Department Supervisor confirms whether late arrival was communicated in advance (SMS, call, team messaging app); system auto-calculates deduction per company policy — grace period: 15 minutes (no deduction); 16–60 minutes late: 1-hour deduction; &gt;60 minutes late: half-day deduction; if late was due to verified force majeure (MRT breakdown, flooding), HR Supervisor applies excused tardiness with no deduction
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / HR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 3 min/exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W561_Task12" name="For absences: system checks if leave was pre-filed per HR-007 leave management…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: For absences: system checks if leave was pre-filed per HR-007 leave management; if leave filed and approved → no exception (system auto-clears); if leave not filed → classify as absent without pay; if absence due to force majeure (typhoon signal, declared calamity) → classify per company policy as excused with pay (up to 5 days/year) or special emergency leave per DOLE advisory
Responsible (R): HR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min/exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W561_Task13" name="For undertime: verify if early departure was authorized by Department…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: For undertime: verify if early departure was authorized by Department Supervisor (system checks for approved early departure request); if authorized → no deduction, update timesheet; if unauthorized → system deducts proportional hours from daily pay; pattern detection: employee with &gt;3 unauthorized undertime incidents in 30 days flagged for Store Manager counseling
Responsible (R): HR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 3 min/exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W561_Task14" name="For missing punches: employee submits self-service correction request via HR…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: For missing punches: employee submits self-service correction request via HR portal or mobile app with reason (forgot to punch, system down, was at other location for task); Department Supervisor approves or denies within 2 business days; if approved → system creates corrected punch entry with audit trail; if denied → exception remains and standard deduction applies
Responsible (R): Employee / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): HR Supervisor
Duration: 2 min/exception (system); 5 min if manual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W561_Task15" name="For unauthorized overtime: system verifies against pre-approved overtime per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: For unauthorized overtime: system verifies against pre-approved overtime per W34 shift schedule; if OT was pre-approved → clear exception, system calculates OT pay (125% regular, 130% rest day, per Labor Code); if unapproved → flag for Store Manager review — Store Manager decides whether to approve retroactively (with justification) or deny (OT hours not compensated); pattern detection: employee with repeated unapproved OT flagged for counseling
Responsible (R): HR Supervisor / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min/exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W561_Task16" name="Mass exception handling (typhoon, transportation strike, widespread flooding)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Mass exception handling (typhoon, transportation strike, widespread flooding): CHRO issues blanket excused attendance directive per DOLE advisory — specifies affected areas, dates, and pay treatment (excused with pay, offset against leave credits, or no-pay); system applies mass exception clearance for all affected employees in specified locations; no individual review required for covered exceptions
Responsible (R): CHRO
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 1–2 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W561_Task17" name="Approved exceptions update payroll input file for W10: system generates…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Approved exceptions update payroll input file for W10: system generates corrected attendance file with all resolved exceptions reflected; unresolved exceptions (pending supervisor approval) carry forward to next payroll cutoff with default deduction applied; exceptions resolved after payroll run trigger retroactive adjustment in next payroll period
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (daily sync)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W561_Task18" name="Weekly exception trend analysis: HR Supervisor generates exception trend report…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Weekly exception trend analysis: HR Supervisor generates exception trend report by store, department, and category; identifies: stores with exception rates &gt;20% (above company average), repeat offenders (&gt;5 exceptions/month), exception categories trending upward; report shared with Store Manager and HR Business Partner for corrective action
Responsible (R): HR Supervisor
Accountable (A): HR Business Partner
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W561_Task19" name="Monthly attendance compliance report: aggregated exception data feeds into W72…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: Monthly attendance compliance report: aggregated exception data feeds into W72 (employee performance — attendance scorecard component) and W67 (store performance — labor compliance metric); stores with exception rates &gt;20% for 2 consecutive months flagged for HR Business Partner intervention; annual attendance compliance data supports DOLE labor standards audit documentation
Responsible (R): HR Supervisor
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W561_Flow35</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W561_End20" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W561_Flow35</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W561_Annotation21">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-298 (ensure controlled execution — Workforce Management (PA-19.3).) | - operational: IT preventive maintenance schedule per W48 and alternative punch methods (RFID badge backup); operational: automated mass exception clearance (step 9); operational: mobile app simplification and associate training
Owner: HR Supervisor / Store Manager (store-level)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
