    <bpmn:process id="W_W1032" name="W1032. Employee Overtime Pre-Approval, Monitoring &amp; DOLE Weekly Cap Enforcement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Employee schedule extends beyond 8 hours/day; department overtime budget threshold reached; weekly overtime limit approaching
Frequency: Daily monitoring across 6,911 employees; weekly reporting
Volume: ~15–25% of store employees work overtime weekly (particularly during peak: payday weekends, bi-monthly sales, holiday season)
Owner: Store Manager (store-level); HR Business Partner (HQ)
Participants: Department Supervisor, Employee, HR Payroll Specialist, DOLE Compliance Officer
Source: workflow W1032 — Employee Overtime Pre-Approval, Monitoring &amp; DOLE Weekly Cap Enforcement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1032_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1032_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1032_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1032_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1032_Lane2" name="Department Supervisors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1032_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1032_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1032_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1032_Lane4" name="Payroll Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1032_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1032_Lane5" name="HR Business Partner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1032_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1032_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1032_Start7" name="Employee schedule extends beyond 8 hours/day; department overtime budget threshold…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1032_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1032_Task8" name="Weekly Overtime Budget Allocation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly Overtime Budget Allocation: Weekly (Monday): (a) Store Manager reviews upcoming week&#x27;s overtime demand forecast based on: promotional events per W83 (bi-monthly sale → higher foot traffic → more cashiers and floor staff), delivery schedule per W109 (2–3 trucks/week → receiving clerk overtime), inventory events per W6 (cycle count schedule), and seasonal peaks per W577 (ber-months) and W578 (payday weekends); (b) Store Manager allocates overtime budget per department in hours: total weekly overtime budget = store labor budget (5% of weekly payroll as guideline) distributed across departments based on expected need; (c) Department Supervisors submit overtime requests for their teams: employee name, date, hours needed, reason; (d) Store Manager approves, reduces, or denies overtime requests; (e) system records approved overtime hours per employee per week with running total
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Department Supervisors
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 20–30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1032_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1032_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1032_Task9" name="Daily Pre-Approval &amp; Real-Time Monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Daily Pre-Approval &amp; Real-Time Monitoring: On the day: (a) if overtime is pre-planned (approved in step 1): employee works beyond shift end per approved schedule; system tracks actual hours vs. approved hours; (b) if unplanned overtime is needed (emergency situation: late truck arrival, unexpected customer volume): Department Supervisor requests overtime approval from Store Manager via mobile app with reason code; Store Manager approves or denies in real-time; (c) system monitors real-time overtime accumulation: (i) daily tracker: employee has worked X hours today (8-hour regular + Y overtime); system alerts at 10 hours (approaching 12-hour daily cap) and blocks at 12 hours (cannot clock additional time); (ii) weekly tracker: employee has accumulated X overtime hours this week; system alerts at 6 hours (approaching 8-hour weekly soft cap) and flags at 8 hours (requires Store Manager justification and HR Business Partner notification); (d) biometric system enforces: employee cannot clock in earlier than scheduled shift start or clock out later than approved overtime end without manager override
Responsible (R): Department Supervisors / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min/day (monitoring)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1032_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1032_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1032_Task10" name="Overtime Cost Tracking &amp; Labor Budget Control">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Overtime Cost Tracking &amp; Labor Budget Control: Daily/weekly: (a) system calculates overtime cost per employee: (regular hourly rate × overtime hours × premium factor based on day type: 125% regular-day OT, 169% rest-day OT, 260% regular-holiday OT); (b) system aggregates: daily overtime cost per department, per store, and cumulative weekly overtime cost vs. budget; (c) Store Manager receives daily overtime cost flash report: total overtime hours, cost, % of weekly budget consumed; (d) if overtime exceeds 80% of weekly budget by mid-week (Wednesday): Store Manager must take corrective action: reduce Thursday–Friday overtime, redeploy staff from low-traffic to high-traffic departments, or request overtime budget increase from District Manager per W1030 with justification; (e) Finance Analyst monitors overtime as % of total labor cost per store per W602 (Store-Level Labor Cost Monitoring); target: overtime ≤ 5% of total store payroll
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min/day (report review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1032_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1032_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1032_Task11" name="DOLE Compliance Reporting &amp; Audit Trail">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: DOLE Compliance Reporting &amp; Audit Trail: Monthly: (a) HR Payroll Specialist generates overtime compliance report per store: (i) total overtime hours per employee, (ii) overtime premium paid, (iii) any instances of &gt; 8 hours overtime/week per employee, (iv) any instances of &gt; 12 hours work in a single day, (v) any employee who refused overtime (consent documentation); (b) exceptions (employees exceeding 8 hours overtime/week) must have documented justification: business reason, Store Manager approval, and employee consent acknowledgment; (c) HR Business Partner reviews exception reports and coaches Store Managers who consistently exceed overtime targets; (d) DOLE inspection readiness: overtime records (timesheets, approval forms, premium payment proof) maintained for 3 years per DOLE record retention requirement; (e) system maintains audit trail: overtime request → approval → actual hours worked → premium calculation → payroll payment → DOLE report
Responsible (R): Payroll Specialist / HR Business Partner
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1032_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1032_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1032_Task12" name="Overtime Reduction &amp; Workforce Optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Overtime Reduction &amp; Workforce Optimization: Quarterly: (a) HR Business Partner and Store Manager analyze overtime patterns: (i) which departments consistently exceed overtime budget? (ii) which days/shifts generate the most overtime? (iii) is overtime caused by understaffing, poor scheduling, or operational inefficiency? (b) corrective strategies: (i) Understaffing: adjust headcount per store staffing model (29 per store); evaluate if store needs additional part-time or seasonal staff per W555; (ii) Poor scheduling: optimize shift start/end times to align with customer traffic patterns per W34; (iii) Operational inefficiency: identify process bottlenecks (slow receiving, inefficient cycle counting) and improve via cross-training per W1042 or process redesign; (c) benchmark overtime across 200 stores: identify best-practice stores with lowest overtime and highest productivity; share learnings via DM network per W1030
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / Store Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–3 hours/quarter per store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1032_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1032_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1032_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1032_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1032_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-298 (ensure controlled execution — Workforce Management (PA-19.3).) | - operational: must be the sole time-tracking mechanism; operational: must flag managers whose stores consistently exceed overtime budgets for HR review; operational: should flag employees working &gt; 6 consecutive days without rest day
Owner: Store Manager (store-level); HR Business Partner (HQ)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1032_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1032_Annotation14" targetRef="W1032_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
