    <bpmn:process id="W_W1182" name="W1182. Multi-Entity Cross-Company Workforce Scheduling &amp; Labor Cost Allocation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly payroll processing cycle; or employee transfer between entities; or management re-allocation of shared services headcount
Frequency: Monthly during payroll; as-needed for intercompany transfers
Volume: 6,911 employees across 5 legal entities; ~50–80 intercompany cost allocations/month
Owner: HR Operations Manager / Finance Controller
Participants: HR Operations Manager, Finance Controller, Department Heads, Payroll Administrator, Tax Accountant
Source: workflow W1182 — Multi-Entity Cross-Company Workforce Scheduling &amp; Labor Cost Allocation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1182_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1182_Lane1" name="HR Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1182_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1182_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1182_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1182_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1182_Lane2" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1182_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1182_Lane3" name="Payroll Administrator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1182_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1182_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1182_Start5" name="Monthly payroll processing cycle; or employee transfer between entities; or management…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1182_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1182_Task6" name="Entity assignment at hire">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Entity assignment at hire: HR Operations Manager assigns new hire to employing entity per offer letter: (a) store employees → BuildRight Depot, Inc.; (b) DC employees → BuildRight Logistics, Inc.; (c) ecommerce employees → BuildRight Digital Commerce, Inc.; (d) property/facility employees → BuildRight Property Management, Inc.; (e) HQ shared services → BuildRight Holdings, Inc.; (f) system records employing entity for payroll, tax, and benefits administration per W15 onboarding
Responsible (R): HR Operations Manager
Accountable (A): Department Head
Duration: Per W15</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1182_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1182_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1182_Task7" name="Shared services cost allocation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Shared services cost allocation: Monthly, Finance Controller allocates shared services headcount costs across benefiting entities: (a) determine allocation basis: (i) IT: system users per entity, (ii) HR: employee count per entity, (iii) Finance: transaction volume per entity, (iv) Legal: hours per entity; (b) calculate monthly intercompany service fee = employee salary + benefits + overhead × allocation percentage; (c) book intercompany journal entries per W87 intercompany elimination; (d) shared services employees remain employed by Holdings; intercompany charges are service fees, not employment costs
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1182_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1182_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1182_Task8" name="Cross-entity temporary deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Cross-entity temporary deployment: When employees temporarily support another entity (e.g., DC surge labor from store staff during Ber months): (a) originating entity retains employer status — employee remains on originating entity&#x27;s payroll; (b) Finance charges receiving entity for temporary labor at cost + 10% administration fee (arm&#x27;s length); (c) track hours worked per entity via timekeeping system; (d) ensure total hours comply with DOLE maximum hours per week per W1032; (e) temporary deployment limited to 3 months; longer assignments require formal transfer per Step 4
Responsible (R): HR Operations Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 hours/deployment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1182_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1182_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1182_Task9" name="Formal intercompany transfer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Formal intercompany transfer: When employee permanently moves between entities: (a) HR processes termination from originating entity and re-hire by receiving entity (Philippine labor law treats this as new employment); (b) process final pay from originating entity: unused leave, 13th-month pro-rata, tax clearance; (c) clear SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG transfers — employee retains same numbers but employer changes; (d) re-onboard employee at receiving entity per W15 (simplified, as internal transfer); (e) Finance processes asset transfer for any company property (laptop, phone, vehicle); (f) update org chart and reporting structure in HR system
Responsible (R): HR Operations Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Per transfer</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1182_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1182_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1182_Task10" name="Payroll reconciliation across entities">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Payroll reconciliation across entities: Monthly payroll reconciliation per W40 payroll cycle: (a) each entity processes payroll independently (separate BIR TIN registrations, separate SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG employer numbers); (b) Finance consolidates total company payroll cost for management reporting; (c) verify intercompany labor charges net to zero on consolidation per W87; (d) total SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG contributions verified per entity; (e) BIR withholding tax per entity reconciled to monthly remittance per W90
Responsible (R): Payroll Administrator / Finance
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2 days/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1182_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1182_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1182_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1182_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1182_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-298 (ensure controlled execution — Workforce Management (PA-19.3).) | - operational: formal transfer handling per Step 4 to maintain employee morale
Owner: HR Operations Manager / Finance Controller</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1182_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1182_Annotation12" targetRef="W1182_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
