    <bpmn:process id="W_W1357" name="W1357. Store Shift Optimization Based on Foot Traffic Analytics &amp; Sales Pattern Analysis" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly shift optimization review cycle; or significant change in store traffic pattern (new competitor, road construction affecting access, residential development nearby)
Frequency: Monthly review per store; quarterly deep analysis across all 200 stores
Volume: 200 stores × monthly review; each store has 2–3 shifts/day × 29 employees
Owner: Regional Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Regional Manager, HR Workforce Analyst, VP Store Operations
Source: workflow W1357 — Store Shift Optimization Based on Foot Traffic Analytics &amp; Sales Pattern Analysis</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1357_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1357_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1357_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1357_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1357_Lane2" name="HR Workforce Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1357_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1357_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1357_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1357_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1357_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1357_Lane4" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1357_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1357_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1357_Start6" name="Monthly shift optimization review cycle; or significant change in store traffic pattern…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1357_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1357_Task7" name="System generates monthly foot traffic heat map per store using POS transaction…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System generates monthly foot traffic heat map per store using POS transaction timestamps (proxy for traffic), CCTV analytics (where available), and loyalty card scan data
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1357_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1357_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1357_Task8" name="HR Workforce Analyst produces shift coverage vs. traffic overlay: compares…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: HR Workforce Analyst produces shift coverage vs. traffic overlay: compares current shift schedule against traffic pattern to identify understaffed peak hours and overstaffed troughs
Responsible (R): HR Workforce Analyst
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month per region</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1357_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1357_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1357_Task9" name="Store Manager provides qualitative input on local factors: school schedules…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Store Manager provides qualitative input on local factors: school schedules, market day patterns, construction project timelines, fiesta dates, and road conditions affecting customer arrival times
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1357_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1357_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1357_Task10" name="Regional Manager reviews shift coverage analysis for all stores in region…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Regional Manager reviews shift coverage analysis for all stores in region (Mindanao: 60 stores, Visayas: 40, Luzon regions: 20–50 each); approves schedule adjustments
Responsible (R): Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4–6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1357_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1357_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1357_Task11" name="Store Manager implements approved shift adjustments in scheduling system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Store Manager implements approved shift adjustments in scheduling system; reassigns Sales Associates and Cashiers to match optimized coverage
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1357_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1357_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1357_Task12" name="Quarterly deep analysis: HR Workforce Analyst measures impact of shift changes…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly deep analysis: HR Workforce Analyst measures impact of shift changes on sales per labor hour, customer satisfaction scores, and overtime hours; recommends further adjustments
Responsible (R): HR Workforce Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1357_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1357_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1357_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1357_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1357_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-298 (ensure controlled execution — Workforce Management (PA-19.3).) | - operational: rest day (1 per 6 consecutive days) constrains how shifts can be stacked during peak periods
Owner: Regional Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
