    <bpmn:process id="W_W5498" name="W5498. Telecommuting &amp; Flexible / Hybrid Work Arrangement Program (RA 11165)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Employee/department application for a telecommuting or hybrid arrangement; (b) program design and annual review cycle; (c) agreement expiry
Frequency: Continuous arrangement administration; eligibility windows 2×/year; agreement renewals annual
Volume: Eligible population ≈ 400–500 roles (HQ corporate functions (~511 active staff, profile §3.3/§11.1 — HQ 511 active of the TO&#x27;s 532-role design, Trade / Account Management disabled — prepared 2026-09-23 (x), the TPS build squad deferred — prepared (ad) and the OMO build squad deferred — prepared (ah), sourcing register §4 amendments, registry CAP-B01; promoted 2026-09-14; gap-filled 2026-09-18) plus portable regional-office and analytics roles); target participation 50–150 active arrangements (~1–2% of 6,911 employees — store, DC, field, and customer-facing roles are structurally ineligible, which the program must communicate to preserve frontline equity)
Owner: HR Manager
Participants: Employee, Department Head, IT (equipment/VPN/MDM — VS-27/VS-99), OSH Officer (home workstation — VS-24), Payroll (VS-19.2), Legal, Facilities (desk-sharing — VS-138)
Source: workflow W5498 — Telecommuting &amp; Flexible / Hybrid Work Arrangement Program (RA 11165)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5498_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5498_Lane1" name="HR Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5498_Lane2" name="IT">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5498_Lane3" name="Employee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5498_Lane4" name="Dept Head">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5498_Lane5" name="Payroll">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5498_Lane6" name="OSH Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5498_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5498_Start8" name="(a) Employee/department application for a telecommuting or hybrid arrangement; (b)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5498_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5498_Task9" name="Program framework per RA 11165 + IRR: eligibility criteria (role portability…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Program framework per RA 11165 + IRR: eligibility criteria (role portability, completed probation, performance standing), arrangement menu (full-remote, hybrid with fixed on-site days, flexi-hours around core hours), the no-less-favorable-treatment principle (pay, benefits, training, promotion), and frontline-equity rationale; CHRO approval
Responsible (R): HR Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 10–15 days (initial); 2–3 days/annual refresh</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5498_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5498_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5498_Task10" name="Written telecommuting agreement per the Act: schedule and core hours, duties…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Written telecommuting agreement per the Act: schedule and core hours, duties and deliverables, probationary arrangement period, equipment/allowance terms, OSH and data-protection obligations, duration, and termination/return-to-office conditions; generated from template and executed with e-signature in the HRIS (records per VS-88)
Responsible (R): HR Manager / Employee / Dept Head
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 1–2 hrs/arrangement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5498_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5498_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5498_Task11" name="Equipment &amp; connectivity setup: IT issues laptop with VPN/MDM enrollment and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Equipment &amp; connectivity setup: IT issues laptop with VPN/MDM enrollment and multi-factor authentication (VS-27.2), updates the IT asset register (VS-99), and confirms bandwidth minimums; allowance treatment confirmed against VS-102 benefit design
Responsible (R): IT / Employee
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 1–3 days/arrangement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5498_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5498_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5498_Task12" name="Home-workstation OSH assessment: employee completes the ergonomic/electrical…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Home-workstation OSH assessment: employee completes the ergonomic/electrical self-assessment checklist; OSH Officer reviews virtually and addresses deficiencies (chair, lighting, outlets, escape path) — the employer&#x27;s RA 11165 OSH duty at the telework site; recorded in the OSH file (VS-24)
Responsible (R): Employee / OSH Officer
Accountable (A): OSH Officer
Duration: 1–2 hrs/arrangement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5498_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5498_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5498_Task13" name="Attendance &amp; timekeeping integration: remote clock-in/clock-out via ESS with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Attendance &amp; timekeeping integration: remote clock-in/clock-out via ESS with the same exception handling as on-site staff (W594/W561); overtime requires the same prior approval and DOLE weekly-cap enforcement as on-site roles (W1032); schedule changes flow to the shift plan (W34)
Responsible (R): Employee / Dept Head
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 15 min/month/arrangement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5498_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5498_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5498_Task14" name="Performance management on outputs: KPIs and deliverables recorded in the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Performance management on outputs: KPIs and deliverables recorded in the performance system (W72 pattern); weekly manager 1:1 cadence; hybrid team norms (meeting equity for remote participants) documented at department level
Responsible (R): Dept Head / Employee
Accountable (A): Dept Head&#x27;s VP
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5498_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5498_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5498_Task15" name="Data protection &amp; security compliance: clean-desk and no-shared-device rules…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Data protection &amp; security compliance: clean-desk and no-shared-device rules, VPN-only system access, printing restrictions, screen-privacy practice, and prompt incident reporting (VS-91/W53 pattern); annual security-awareness completion tracked (VS-27)
Responsible (R): Employee / IT Security
Accountable (A): IT Manager
Duration: 30 min/year/arrangement + continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5498_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5498_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5498_Task16" name="Allowance &amp; payroll treatment: telecommuting allowance posted as the configured…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Allowance &amp; payroll treatment: telecommuting allowance posted as the configured payroll wage type with BIR tax treatment per VS-19.2 statutory rules; de-minimis assessment documented with Finance
Responsible (R): Payroll / HR Manager
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 30 min/arrangement + annual review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5498_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5498_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5498_Task17" name="Telework accident handling: injuries in the course of telework are documented…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Telework accident handling: injuries in the course of telework are documented and filed as EC claims under PD 626 like on-site injuries (W805); OSH Officer maintains the telework incident log
Responsible (R): OSH Officer / HR
Accountable (A): OSH Officer
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5498_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5498_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5498_Task18" name="Program review &amp; compliance readiness: annual policy review; DOLE…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Program review &amp; compliance readiness: annual policy review; DOLE labor-standards inspection readiness (agreements, payslips, OSH records — VS-22.2); participation/attrition/productivity analytics; agreement renewals and terminations; desk-ratio and workplace feedback to Facilities (VS-138)
Responsible (R): HR Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 3–5 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5498_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5498_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5498_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5498_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5498_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-298 (ensure controlled execution — Workforce Management (PA-19.3).)
Owner: HR Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
