    <bpmn:process id="W_W5532" name="W5532. Workforce Time &amp; Attendance (Biometric/Time-Clock) Platform Estate &amp; Punch-Data Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Shift start/end generating punch events at ~205 stores, 4 DCs and HQ; a device-offline alert or punch-interface failure; a new-store/DC opening or closure requiring device provisioning or decommissioning (W16/W703); a payroll cut-off requiring the final punch-data interface run (W10/W816); or the periodic device-health and data-retention review
Frequency: Continuous event collection; scheduled interface runs ahead of every payroll cut-off; monthly device-health review; event-driven provisioning/decommissioning
Volume: ~6,911 employees × ~2 punches × ~250 workdays ≈ 3.2–3.6M punch events/year across a fleet of ~420–450 biometric/RFID time-clock devices (2 per store average, DC gate banks, HQ terminals); ~800–1,200 attendance exceptions/day already processed in W561&#x27;s queues; ~26 payroll interfaces/year (bi-monthly per entity across 5 entities, W816 consolidation scope); ~10–15 store openings/closures/year with provisioning events
Owner: HR Technology Manager
Participants: HR Supervisor, Payroll Specialist, Store Manager, DC Supervisor, IT Service Desk (device break/fix), IT Network Operations (connectivity), VS-103.3 people-data integration (W3350/W3351), External T&amp;A/biometric vendor (maintenance contract)
Source: workflow W5532 — Workforce Time &amp; Attendance (Biometric/Time-Clock) Platform Estate &amp; Punch-Data Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5532_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5532_Lane1" name="HR Technology Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5532_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5532_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5532_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5532_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5532_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5532_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5532_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5532_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5532_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5532_Start4" name="Shift start/end generating punch events at ~205 stores, 4 DCs and HQ; a device-offline…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5532_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5532_Task5" name="Device-fleet registry &amp; health monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Device-fleet registry &amp; health monitoring: maintain the T&amp;A device registry (site, device ID, firmware, last successful sync, maintenance-contract and warranty status) for all ~420–450 devices; monitor daily sync-heartbeat dashboards; dispatch failed devices to the IT service desk with vendor field-service escalation; draw from the spare-device pool so no site waits on repair turnaround
Responsible (R): HR Technology Manager / IT Service Desk
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 30–45 min/day monitoring; ~20–40 device incidents/month at 30–60 min each</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5532_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5532_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5532_Task6" name="Punch-data collection &amp; payroll interface operations">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Punch-data collection &amp; payroll interface operations: run the punch-collection interfaces (real-time store feeds plus scheduled batch pulls); deduplicate retries and missing-punch artifacts; validate and land punch files in the payroll staging area ahead of each W10/W816 cut-off; reconcile interface counts (devices reporting vs punches received vs employees scheduled per W34) and rerun on variance
Responsible (R): HR Technology Manager
Accountable (A): Payroll Specialist
Duration: 45–60 min/interface run; reruns add ~30 min on failure</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5532_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5532_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5532_Task7" name="Offline &amp; outage fallback management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Offline &amp; outage fallback management: during device, network or power outages (market-wide power interruptions, typhoon events per W1386), activate the manual-punch fallback with supervisor logs; backfill captured punches when systems restore with supervisor confirmation feeding W561&#x27;s exception queue; track outage-affected sites to closure
Responsible (R): Store Manager / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): HR Supervisor
Duration: event-driven; ~15–30 min/site per outage day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5532_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5532_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5532_Task8" name="Provisioning &amp; decommissioning on the site and employee lifecycle">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Provisioning &amp; decommissioning on the site and employee lifecycle: provision or decommission devices, employee biometric/RFID templates and user-to-device mappings on hire (W15), transfer (W511/W1410), separation (W43) and store opening/closure (W16/W703); enforce template re-enrollment after hand injuries (a hardware-retail frequency event) and template deletion on separation per the RA 10173 retention schedule
Responsible (R): HR Technology Manager
Accountable (A): HR Supervisor
Duration: ~1.5–2 h per store opening/closure event; ~15 min per separation cleanup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5532_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5532_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5532_Task9" name="Downstream integration quality">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Downstream integration quality: reconcile device punches against W34/W1357 shift plans and W1032-approved overtime before payroll posting; maintain pay-code/premium mappings (night differential, holiday, rest-day) with the W10 payroll rules and the W2764 tax-table treatment; feed unresolved discrepancies into W594/W561 exception queues
Responsible (R): HR Technology Manager / Payroll Specialist, Timekeeping &amp; Attendance Analyst
Accountable (A): HR Technology Manager
Duration: 2–3 h per payroll cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5532_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5532_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5532_Task10" name="Governance, retention &amp; audit support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Governance, retention &amp; audit support: enforce punch-data retention per the W256/W2977 labor-records schedule with RA 10173 minimization; produce DOLE labor-standards evidence packs (hours worked, overtime authorizations, premium payments) for inspections and payroll-dispute defense; report quarterly device-health, interface-reliability and exception-rate KPIs to HR Operations
Responsible (R): HR Technology Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: ~10–12 h/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5532_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5532_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5532_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5532_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5532_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-298 (ensure controlled execution — Workforce Management (PA-19.3).) | - operational: a payroll cut-off cannot close while punch-interface reconciliation shows unresolved variances (Payroll Specialist + HR Technology Manager dual sign-off) | - operational: biometric-template enrollment and deletion events are logged and reviewed monthly against hire/separation records
Owner: HR Technology Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5532_Assoc13" sourceRef="W5532_Annotation12" targetRef="W5532_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5532_Flow14" sourceRef="W5532_Start4" targetRef="W5532_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5532_Flow15" sourceRef="W5532_Task5" targetRef="W5532_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5532_Flow16" sourceRef="W5532_Task6" targetRef="W5532_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5532_Flow17" sourceRef="W5532_Task7" targetRef="W5532_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5532_Flow18" sourceRef="W5532_Task8" targetRef="W5532_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5532_Flow19" sourceRef="W5532_Task9" targetRef="W5532_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5532_Flow20" sourceRef="W5532_Task10" targetRef="W5532_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
